## Comparison of $1997^{1998^{1999}}$ and $1999^{1998^{1997}}$

Let
$$A = 1997^{1998^{1999}}, \qquad B = 1999^{1998^{1997}}.$$

Since both are positive, it suffices to compare their natural logarithms:

$$\ln A = 1998^{1999}\ln 1997, \qquad \ln B = 1998^{1997}\ln 1999.$$

Form the ratio:

$$\frac{\ln A}{\ln B} = \frac{1998^{1999}}{1998^{1997}}\cdot\frac{\ln 1997}{\ln 1999} = 1998^{2}\cdot\frac{\ln 1997}{\ln 1999}.$$

Therefore

$$A > B \iff \ln A > \ln B \iff 1998^{2}\ln 1997 > \ln 1999 \iff \ln\!\bigl(1997^{\,1998^{2}}\bigr) > \ln 1999 \iff 1997^{\,1998^{2}} > 1999.$$

Now compute $1998^{2}$:

$$1998^{2} = (2000-2)^{2} = 4\,000\,000 - 8\,000 + 4 = 3\,992\,004.$$

In particular $1998^{2} \geq 2$, so

$$1997^{\,1998^{2}} \geq 1997^{2} = (2000-3)^{2} = 4\,000\,000 - 12\,000 + 9 = 3\,988\,009.$$

Since $3\,988\,009 > 1999$, we have

$$1997^{\,1998^{2}} > 1999.$$

Hence $\ln A > \ln B$, and consequently $A > B$.

### Conclusion

$$\boxed{1997^{1998^{1999}} > 1999^{1998^{1997}}}.$$

The number $1997^{1998^{1999}}$ is larger.

